# AutoCua API keys
#
# Copy this file to .env, then fill in a key for at least one provider:
#   macOS / Linux:  cp .env.example .env
#   Windows:        copy .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored, so your keys stay on your machine - never commit them.
# The app's Settings panel saves keys into this same file.

# --- Model providers (one is enough) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=
REQUESTY_API_KEY=
TOGETHER_API_KEY=

# --- Ollama (a model on this machine: needs no key) ---
# Leave these commented to use the Ollama app on this machine
# (http://127.0.0.1:11434). OLLAMA_HOST points at an Ollama elsewhere
# (host, host:port or a URL); OLLAMA_API_KEY is only for one behind a key.
# OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# --- AWS Bedrock ---
# A Bedrock API key (sent as a Bearer token), not an IAM access key pair.
AWS_API_KEY=
# Bedrock region. Leave commented out to use the default, eu-west-2.
# AWS_BEDROCK_REGION=eu-west-2

# --- Google Vertex AI ---
# Uncomment only if you use Vertex models. Settings saves them here too.
# VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id
# VERTEX_LOCATION=global

# --- iPhone ---
# Optional: the bundle ID prefix pairing signs the AutoCua app with. Unset,
# pairing uses com.AutoCua.<your Apple team ID>, which is yours alone (Apple
# registers a bundle ID to one account). To use your own, set it here (like
# com.yourname) or in Settings > Connect Device > iPhone > Bundle ID.
# IOS_BUNDLE_ID_PREFIX=com.yourname

# --- Telegram remote control ---
# Connect the bot in the app's Settings, which saves TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN here.
